From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Dago <ydago@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:50:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/48] [net][policy] Add AllHttpAuthSchemesAllowedForProxies
 policy

Adds the AllHttpAuthSchemesAllowedForProxies enterprise policy, allowing
administrators to explicitly configure proxy servers that may use all
HTTP authentication schemes regardless of AuthSchemes.

This CL:
- Defines and registers the AllHttpAuthSchemesAllowedForProxies policy
  and auth.http_auth_allowed_for_proxies pref.
- Binds patterns_allowed_to_use_all_schemes_for_proxies to the new
  policy when set in SystemNetworkContextManager, falling back to
  AllHttpAuthSchemesAllowedForOrigins when under M161.
- Adds policy pref mapping tests.

Bug: 533454968
Change-Id: I4eb7c4287ad7af8afa565bfc0e9e26ef471e2ea4
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8456427
Reviewed-by: Sebastien Lalancette <seblalancette@chromium.org>
